From: dotlouis <1891109+dotlouis@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 11:31:37 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 23/41] MTROPOLIS: Resolve object paths stored in string
 variables

Uncle Albert's Fabulous Voyage keeps references to notebook objects in
string variables: it assigns an object to a string variable, and reads
the object back with the variable's "object" attribute.

Move the object path resolution of object reference variables to a new
Runtime::resolveObjectPath(), which handles absolute and relative paths
and loads scenes on the way. Assigning an object to a string variable
now stores the object's absolute path, and the "object" attribute of a
string variable resolves its path.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
